WEBVTT

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:03.290
<i>Having enrolled in Enoshima High,</i>

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:06.690
<i>I met Araki-san, who was so fat he 
looked like a different person,</i>

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:10.380
<i>and through a strange series of events, 
I joined the play-for-fun FC club.</i>

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:14.440
<i>There is also an official club 
called SC at this school,</i>

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:15.670
<i>against whom the FC will compete</i>

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:18.650
<i>with the representation of 
the school on the line.</i>

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.560
<i>Spurred by the desire to defeat SC,</i>

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.180
<i>we practice every day 
until the sun goes down.</i>

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.290
<i>Araki-san, however, 
never showed up</i>

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:29.520
<i>and the day of the match arrived.</i>

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:06.020
<b>Clash! FC vs. SC!!</b>

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.760
Those guys are as huge as always.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:34.800
While in comparison...

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.590
You guys gonna be all right?

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:41.190
Probably.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:43.220
Don't overdo it and hurt yourself.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:47.430
Unlike the other team, 
we just barely have 11 players.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:49.890
So then, Araki-san isn't...

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:58.860
More importantly, 
let's focus on the game at hand.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:03.320
Let's show them what the FC is made of.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:14.460
Coach Kondo,

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:18.000
allow me to learn from 
you again this year.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:21.640
As if that's really your intent.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:23.010
I can see in your eyes that you're trying

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.890
to frustrate my plans, Iwaki-kun.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:27.890
Yes, that's exactly right.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.680
The chance of us losing is less 
than one in ten thousand.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.510
We cannot allow that to happen.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:36.820
Ever.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.740
School Representation Deciding Match

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.740
Hey, how about over there?

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:51.410
To a good match.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.920
Do your best this year, FC!

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.580
Don't lose, SC!

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.300
It's that time of year again,

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.020
when we find out which team will earn

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:01.260
the right to represent the school.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:13.390
Enoshima Broadcasting Club

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.700
Who is going to win this match?

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.050
Covering this game will be me,

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.370
from the Enoshima Broadcasting Club,

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:09.090
Ichiro Yamanashi and...

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.280
Momoko Fukushima—

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.650
Let's get right to 
introducing the players.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:14.400
Starting with SC...

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.520
Enoshima High School

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.520
Soccer Club

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:21.930
The goal keeper, Shintaro Todo.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:23.770
On defense from the left side,

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:25.050
Kenji Fudo,

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:26.310
Go Kaiouji,

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.570
Shigeru Wakamura.

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:31.520
Defensive midfielders, Shuji Sakamoto,

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:32.890
Ryoma Oda.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:35.690
Offensive midfielders from the left side,

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:37.010
Kazuma Nakamura,

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.280
in the middle, second row,

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:39.470
Yuji Sawamura,

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:40.570
on the right side,

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:41.780
Koji Yakumo.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:43.520
Finally, the forwards,

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:45.830
Kenya Kudo and Michiro Takase

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.380
in a two-top formation.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:51.190
We'll have to keep an eye 
on these four players.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.720
The second year, number 10, 
and cornerstone of the team,

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:54.620
Oda!

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:57.860
Standing at 190 centimeters tall, 
equipped with the powerful headers

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.550
that come with that height,

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:01.650
the enormous forward, 
first year, Takase.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.580
Physically the strongest on the team,

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:07.000
the powerful defender, 
second year, Kaiouji.

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:09.840
Finally, the conductor for the team,

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.040
the captain, third year, Sawamura.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:14.650
The opposing FC's starting lineup is...

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:15.160
Enoshima High School

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:15.160
Football Club

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.260
Goal keeper, Reo Kurebayashi.

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:22.540
On defense, from the left side,

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:24.320
Shinji Mikami,

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:25.570
Akito Horikawa,

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:26.780
Yutaka Nishigoori.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.500
The defensive midfielders, 
Manabu Sakurai,

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:30.660
Yukizo Hama.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:33.400
In the second row, Makoto Hyodo,

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.520
Koji Endo,

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:36.060
Kaoru Matoba.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.310
Finally, in two-top position,

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:40.150
Junpei Hino and Kakeru Aizawa.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.900
The players to take note 
of on this team are...

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.100
Wait, really?

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:47.250
There aren't any?

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:47.910
I see.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:52.010
That's so mean...

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:53.380
It can't be helped,

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:56.160
but if we win this match, 
our roles will reverse.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:57.120
Yeah.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.580
It's now time for the kick-off.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.160
<i>Here I go, Brother.</i>

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.820
<i>It's too bad that Araki-san isn't here,</i>

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:12.270
<i>but, if we win, I'm sure he'll come back.</i>

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:15.560
<i>In that sense as well,
 I can't afford to lose this match.</i>

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:18.690
FC moves right into an attack.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:19.670
Jersey number 9,

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:21.110
Aizawa, is on the move.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.550
Don't let them get a pass to number 9.

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:24.570
Keep them to the sides.

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:33.530
<i>Kakeru...</i>

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:35.300
Whoops.

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:37.710
Hyodo,

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:39.670
you're a midfielder?

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:41.630
So Araki never came back?

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:44.140
Don't worry, Sawamura-san.

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:47.000
Even without him, our strength,

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.510
compared to last year,

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:49.720
is on a different level!

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:56.640
Shit. Fudo, block the pass route!

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:57.850
On it!

00:06:58.770 --> 00:06:59.890
I'll take that.

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:03.430
Hino-san.

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:05.270
All right!

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:08.780
Oh, and forward number 11,

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:10.780
Hino, takes the ball.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:13.280
Yes! Looking good, everyone!

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:16.130
It's just like we practiced. 
Right, Coach?

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:18.850
Yes. Having Kakeru pull the defense

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:20.460
toward him using tricky moves,

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:22.520
while Hino-kun, now lightly defended,

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:23.920
breaks for the left side.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:26.350
However, the problem lies ahead.

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:29.720
Except for the enormous Takase-kun,

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:32.310
their remaining 9 players are all 
pulled back on their side of the field.

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:36.180
To break through this tight 
formation won't be easy.

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:41.490
If only we had another offensive 
hand to play on the left side,

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:44.980
we could use our physically 
strong Hino-kun on the inside.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:48.540
That's true, however...

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:50.650
Yes. In any case, 
this is our chance.

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:53.410
It's all yours, Mako!

00:07:58.150 --> 00:07:59.550
<i>Bring it on.</i>

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:01.540
<i>If you think you can break 
through this iron wall,</i>

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:02.830
<i>why don't you try?</i>

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:04.790
As if!

00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:06.280
Go!

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:08.350
FC's Hyodo

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:11.260
aims a cross over the heads of 
the defenders to the far side,

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.180
but no one's there to receive it!

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.590
Ha, fool.

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:16.650
Wait, there is one player!

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:18.220
It's Aizawa Kakeru.

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:18.980
<i>All right!</i>

00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:20.560
Kakeru!

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:21.520
What?!

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:23.170
Don't get flustered!

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:25.360
All they got was a lucky pass.

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:26.480
Stay in formation!

00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:28.760
<i>That wasn't luck.</i>

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:30.850
<i>Mako-kun knew very well</i>

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:33.040
<i>that Kakeru-kun's natural intuition</i>

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:34.980
<i>would pull him towards the goal.</i>

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:36.410
<i>Go, Kakeru!</i>

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:37.870
Finish it, Kakeru!

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:45.240
It's mine!

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.050
Look at that!

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:53.500
What an amazing jump!

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:55.050
Number 2, Kaiouji, clears the ball

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:57.540
before it can reach the far side.

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:59.050
Don't get cocky, freshman.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:02.020
<i>And I thought I was completely free...</i>

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:05.350
This isn't good.

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:10.070
Oda clears the ball...

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.430
Wait, no.

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:13.820
It's a long pass to Takase!

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:16.280
Oh no! Everyone get back!

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:19.520
Wow! From that distance 
he was able to predict

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:22.450
Takase's movement and make 
such an accurate pass...

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:25.320
<i>Oda is the team's key player.</i>

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:29.460
<i>Without his accurate long feeds, 
our strategy wouldn't hold together.</i>

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:30.920
Nice, Oda-san!

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:33.150
Don't leave him open.

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:34.260
Stop him, Kaoru.

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:35.340
Got it!

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:46.010
You're tiny.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:48.690
You!

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:51.270
You think being tall is everything?

00:09:58.690 --> 00:09:59.820
Shoot!

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:02.280
<i>He was bait?</i>

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:03.540
Mark number 9!

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:07.710
Too slow! It's mine!

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.170
Kudo shoots!

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:09.960
<i>Right!</i>

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.560
The keeper, Kurebayashi, dives...

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:14.880
...and hits the ball...

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:18.300
...but it's still heading for the goal!

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:22.400
Clear! Clear! Clear!

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:24.080
Running back to the goal,

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:28.980
Aizawa manages to save 
the ball by inches!

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:31.940
Good work, Kakeru!
 Keep it up!

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:33.400
Nice clear.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:38.620
That kid!

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:43.020
Don't get excited. 
We aren't even serious yet.

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:44.080
Got it.

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:48.000
There's 20 minutes left in the half.

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:52.010
Hold on. They're coming back 
with a counterattack.

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:53.170
As if!

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:03.650
Clear! It's clear!

00:11:03.650 --> 00:11:06.270
Again, the forward, Aizawa, returns.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:07.220
Man, again?

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:10.330
However, with both forwards 
being kept on the defense,

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:12.190
FC is starting to look tired.

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:18.170
Ichiro Yamanashi           Momoko Fukushima

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:15.450
This is rather one-sided.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:18.560
It would appear that 
the absence of number 10,

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:22.160
last year's ace Ryuichi Araki,
 is significantly affecting the team.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:25.620
To think that the king's absence 
would leave this large a hole.

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:28.120
Coach, isn't there anything we can do?

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:32.580
Well, if we had one or 
two more strong players,

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:35.040
we might be able to come up 
with a breakthrough solution.

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:37.570
Don't lose your mark, Kaoru, Kakeru!

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:38.010
Okay!

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:40.010
<i>No matter what the height difference,</i>

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:42.210
<i>with a tight enough mark, I can clear it.</i>

00:11:42.210 --> 00:11:43.970
<i>As soon as we clear, we'll counter.</i>

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:46.430
<i>We have to score at 
least one point somehow.</i>

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:53.560
Shoot!

00:11:57.700 --> 00:11:59.490
Go!

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:04.370
Goooal!

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.260
With 28 minutes down in the first half,

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:08.600
the tie is finally broken!

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:09.330
All right!

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.380
Nice, Captain!

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:12.790
Keep it up, Sawamura!

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:14.760
Just what you'd expect from SC.

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:16.500
They are against a play-for-fun 
team, after all.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.140
I'm sorry. Because...

00:12:19.770 --> 00:12:21.550
Because I let my mark get away...

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:23.420
Don't worry about it.

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:24.850
There was nothing you could've done.

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:26.470
Let's just take one back!

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.520
Because of me...

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:30.720
Kakeru...

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:32.390
Kakeru...

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:35.940
Only minutes left in the first half.

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.860
SC has already pushed back

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.820
and hardened their defense.

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:40.830
Shit!

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.420
Hino-san!

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:43.150
Okay!

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:47.880
Kakeru! Don't hold onto it!

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:49.330
I'm fine.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:50.790
Kakeru-kun, over here!

00:12:51.070 --> 00:12:52.930
<i>That point was my fault.</i>

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:54.250
<i>I've got to get it back somehow!</i>

00:12:55.820 --> 00:12:56.630
What?

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:00.050
<i>Oda-san!</i>

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:03.840
<i>If I get past Oda-san, 
I'll be in the penalty area.</i>

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:05.550
<i>I'll definitely even the score!</i>

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:08.100
<i>You cannot get past me.</i>

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:09.560
<i>This is because...</i>

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:12.020
Kakeru, no! 
Pass to Matoba-kun!

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:19.400
<i>H-How?</i>

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:21.790
<i>You have a grave weakness.</i>

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:23.800
<i>As long as you don't correct it,</i>

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:25.780
<i>you will never beat me.</i>

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:27.870
Go!

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:30.840
He kicks the ball and it's 
a long shot down the field.

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:32.340
This could be their chance!

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:33.200
Takase!

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:35.660
I won't let you do as you please!

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:41.920
Goooal! It's in!

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:47.470
That's the end of the first half.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:50.990
SC has a comfortable lead at half time,

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:53.100
with a score of 2-0.

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:56.720
<i>Kakeru...</i>

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:14.440
It appears you've 
dislocated your shoulder.

00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:15.870
Let's go to the hospital immediately.

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:19.450
I-I'm fine. 
This is nothing.

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:23.240
You can't play with that arm.

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:25.490
B-But then, we'll only have 10 players.

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:27.550
In a regular match,
 even if a player drops out,

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:29.620
the remaining 10 can still play.

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:30.970
Right, everyone?

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:34.600
What's wrong?

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:36.740
Have you already given 
up after the first half?

00:14:36.740 --> 00:14:39.020
I didn't realize the Enoshima High FC

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:40.740
was such a weak-hearted team.

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:46.040
I'm sorry. This is my fault.

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:47.740
I let two goals through.

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:51.200
No one wants to hear your excuses.

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:54.850
A striker never makes excuses.

00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:56.120
Respond with a goal.

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:00.950
<i>Brother...</i>

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:06.960
Nana-chan is right, Kakeru.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:13.330
Kota, what are you doing here?

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:14.740
And why are you half-naked?

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:16.540
I quit.

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:22.050
Like I said, it was boring over there,

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:24.600
so I quit!

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:27.990
What?!

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:30.950
I'm sorry. I quit. 
Please don't look for me.
 Kota Nakatsuka

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:33.450
What does he think he's doing?

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:35.990
See ya!

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:35.990
That idiot!

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:40.980
Unimportant. Leave him be.

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:42.420
B-But...

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:44.740
It's like the coach says.

00:15:44.740 --> 00:15:46.210
His leaving the team

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:48.550
doesn't change how we play soccer.

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:49.850
Oda...

00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:54.280
So, I'm going to have you 
guys let me join, too.

00:15:55.070 --> 00:15:57.000
It's fine, right, Coach Iwaki?

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:58.530
Of course, we're delighted to have you.

00:15:58.530 --> 00:15:59.730
All right!

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:01.030
Nice to meet you.

00:16:01.030 --> 00:16:02.770
Nice to meet you.
 Nice to meet you!

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:04.990
Man, what a character.

00:16:04.990 --> 00:16:07.160
I like you. You're great!

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:09.110
Nice to meet you.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:13.060
Now we can play together 
again, right, Kakeru?

00:16:13.060 --> 00:16:13.700
Right.

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:20.540
You're tense in the shoulders.

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:22.450
Coach.

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:26.030
You did a great job
 defending in the first half.

00:16:26.030 --> 00:16:29.500
However, you may have stood 
out a little too much.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:31.340
What?

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:35.430
Forwards cannot afford to 
stand out all the time...

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:36.890
Disappear, Kakeru.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:40.160
You stand out too much.

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:42.450
That's why the opponents’ 
marks are always tight.

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:45.310
A forward needs to be able 
to disappear sometimes, too.

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:53.350
The second half kick off of 
the traditional Representation

00:16:53.350 --> 00:16:55.240
Team Match is about to begin.

00:16:55.650 --> 00:16:57.730
Kota-kun, do your best!

00:16:57.730 --> 00:16:59.200
I love you, okay?

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:06.170
Ichiro Yamanashi

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:01.810
Due to an injury,

00:17:01.810 --> 00:17:03.940
the FC right side's Mikami 
will be substituted with...

00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:06.170
Who was it again?

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.170
Kota Nakatsuka

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:09.260
Hey! Stop making a fool out of me!

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:16.860
Oh, that's a foul.

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:19.080
However, what a daring, gutsy play

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:21.170
by the recently subbed Kota Nakatsuka.

00:17:21.170 --> 00:17:23.020
Okay, Kota! Keep up the fight!

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:24.250
Thanks.

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:25.730
Nakatsuka, what was that?

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:29.190
Yakumo, you're subbed for 
Teshigawara. Get off the field.

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:33.240
That's so strict.

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:35.080
Just because he 
got a little hot-headed.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:36.630
Well, the substitution was probably

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:38.450
also to strengthen their defense.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:40.630
Teshigawara-kun is the strong type

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:42.410
and would help buffer their defense.

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:43.810
I see.

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:45.160
Mako-kun.

00:17:45.590 --> 00:17:46.430
Yes?

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:49.570
Junpei, Kota, Reo, Horikawa.

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:57.160
There it goes!

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:59.400
He's sent another long pass 
towards the front of the goal.

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:04.430
When Oda-kun, who has complete 
confidence in the accuracy of his free kick,

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:07.690
sees a short mark on Takase-kun,

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:09.770
he will definitely send a pinpoint kick.

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:12.680
But no matter how tall he may be...

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:14.220
All right. It's mine!

00:18:14.220 --> 00:18:16.880
...no player can reach above a

00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:18.910
keeper who can use his hands.

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:20.920
Once I knew it was coming to you,

00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:22.440
making a save was too easy.

00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:25.470
Go, Mako!

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:27.960
All right. It's time for a comeback!

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:32.530
A counterattack that makes 
me want to buy shares in FC!

00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:35.420
Using the free kick

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:37.380
as bait to lure us in 
and perform a counter.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.260
Nice plan.

00:18:38.770 --> 00:18:42.220
But without any strong moves, 
your counters can't scare us.

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:45.310
We'll see about that!

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:50.320
<i>So they were planning on Hino 
breaking through on the left side,</i>

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:54.510
<i>but the coach has already 
anticipated this development.</i>

00:18:54.510 --> 00:18:56.440
<i>In order to strengthen the 
defense on the sides,</i>

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:58.400
<i>Yakumo was subbed out for Teshigawara!</i>

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:00.320
That's as far as you go, Hino!

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:01.780
<i>Idiot.</i>

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:10.460
Ridiculous! Again to the left?

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:12.170
That's it, newcomer!

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:15.030
Go, Kota-kun!

00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:17.190
That was quite smooth, wasn't it, Coach?

00:19:17.190 --> 00:19:20.870
Yes. The addition of Kota, 
a new attack card,

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:22.610
was quite fortuitous for us.

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:24.890
With this, the physically strong Hino-kun

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:26.370
can push towards the goal.

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:29.100
He will be able to break through 
that iron wall defense.

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:31.610
You traitor!

00:19:31.610 --> 00:19:33.560
<i>That's it for me!</i>

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:35.020
<i>I'm counting on you!</i>

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:38.490
<i>Idiot! How high are you 
putting it, newcomer?</i>

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:40.670
You won't get a shot!

00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:44.660
Matoba's volley shot!

00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:47.620
It was blocked! Blocked!

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.600
The ball rolls towards the open 
space on the opposite side.

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:51.620
Who is going to pick this ball up?

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:53.080
Clear it!

00:19:55.390 --> 00:19:56.890
It's Aizawa!

00:19:56.890 --> 00:19:59.890
Aizawa, who hasn't shown 
himself this whole time,

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:02.520
has suddenly taken control of the ball!

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:06.420
You can disappear for minutes.

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:10.910
Disappear for minutes, 
never even touching the ball.

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:13.180
When the ball rolls 
into the penalty area,

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:15.200
appear only in that instant,

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:17.230
and you'll definitely score a goal.

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:19.540
That's a striker!

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:26.580
Goooal!

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:30.120
First year Kakeru Aizawa's 
bullet shot claims a goal!

00:20:30.320 --> 00:20:33.130
Hurrah! We did it, Kakeru!

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:34.330
That was amazing, Kakeru-kun!

00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:38.880
You did it! Amazing, Kakeru!

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:39.960
A striker!

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:44.930
I haven't seen a pure striker 
like him for so long.

00:20:44.930 --> 00:20:46.740
All right. 
Just one more point!

00:20:46.740 --> 00:20:48.600
Let's tie it up!

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:49.890
Yeah!

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:57.700
I'm sorry. If I had marked 
that number 9 properly...

00:20:57.700 --> 00:20:59.050
This is my mistake.

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:00.220
Don't worry about it.

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:02.320
The cause was my amateur free kick.

00:21:02.770 --> 00:21:04.190
Change your attitude.

00:21:04.190 --> 00:21:05.030
Okay.

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:06.300
Fudo, you're subbed.

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:09.540
Can't you hear?
 You're subbed!

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:10.570
Understood.

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:15.050
What? Another sub? 
I don't believe it.

00:21:17.350 --> 00:21:21.550
Thanks to Aizawa's goal, FC has 
narrowed the gap to one point.

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:24.220
Will their momentum carry 
them to tie up the game?

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:24.220
Momoko Fukushima

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:24.220
Currently in the bathroom 
due to too much excitement.

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:25.340
Mako-san!

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:26.340
Kota!

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:27.890
All right!

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:31.690
FC's dizzying passes have 
divided SC's defenders.

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:32.770
Could this be their chance?

00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:34.730
Go, Kakeru!

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.620
<i>Good. We're controlling the 
pace of the second half.</i>

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:40.190
<i>One more point. 
We'll definitely tie it up!</i>

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:44.610
It's mine!

00:21:45.770 --> 00:21:46.610
Oda!

00:21:46.850 --> 00:21:48.070
So close, Hino.

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:49.340
It's up!

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:50.030
This is bad!

00:21:51.820 --> 00:21:52.950
Kudo, to the right!

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:54.410
Crap...

00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:57.510
Nakatsuka was positioned 
a little too far forward.

00:21:57.510 --> 00:21:59.170
He's chasing down Kudo,

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:01.420
who's making a break down the sidelines.

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:03.710
Shit. If it comes to this, 
I'd better foul to stop him!

00:22:07.790 --> 00:22:11.720
You won't be able to put a header 
into the goal like this.

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:13.650
I have no intention of scoring a goal.

00:22:13.650 --> 00:22:14.350
What?

00:22:18.270 --> 00:22:19.750
<i>We've been had!</i>

00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:21.520
<i>I won't let you shoot!</i>

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:30.660
Goooal! SC scores another point!

00:22:30.930 --> 00:22:33.900
The score is now 3-1.

00:22:33.900 --> 00:22:35.090
Damn it...

00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:37.160
<i>What a player.</i>

00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:39.640
<i>If my shot had
 been an instant later,</i>

00:22:39.640 --> 00:22:41.590
<i>there is no doubt he
 would have cleared it.</i>

00:22:42.030 --> 00:22:43.920
<i>In that situation, by himself,</i>

00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:46.590
<i>could he have predicted 
where the ball would be?</i>

00:22:46.590 --> 00:22:49.060
Not yet! It isn't over yet!

00:22:49.060 --> 00:22:51.010
We'll have the last laugh!

00:22:51.620 --> 00:22:52.490
Right!

00:22:59.310 --> 00:23:01.310
Another counter!

00:23:01.310 --> 00:23:02.270
And a shot!

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:04.630
Stopped!

00:23:04.630 --> 00:23:06.810
Only 25 minutes remain.

00:23:06.810 --> 00:23:10.600
FC, two points behind, 
starts to feel the pressure.

00:23:15.260 --> 00:23:16.710
C'mon, FC!

00:23:16.710 --> 00:23:18.080
Fight! Fight!

00:23:34.790 --> 00:23:36.770
Coach, if things keep going...

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:39.860
I know. But don't panic.

00:23:39.860 --> 00:23:42.050
We still have an ace up our sleeve.

00:23:44.930 --> 00:23:47.230
By ace, you don't mean...

00:23:47.230 --> 00:23:50.250
We've been expecting you, King.

00:23:50.250 --> 00:23:53.230
Can you play for the last 20 minutes?

00:23:53.790 --> 00:23:55.020
Obviously.

00:23:55.590 --> 00:23:58.040
That's why I've endured 
waiting in the stands.

00:23:59.140 --> 00:24:01.000
I was surprised. 
I hardly recognized you.

00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:07.710
It's too soon to be surprised.

00:24:10.860 --> 00:24:14.180
Just watch. 
The show's about to begin.

00:24:14.180 --> 00:24:18.680
Number 12, Endo, is substituted 
for number 10, Araki!

00:24:19.080 --> 00:24:20.000
Araki?

00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:20.930
Araki-san?

00:24:21.190 --> 00:24:22.190
Araki!

00:24:22.190 --> 00:24:23.690
Araki.

00:24:23.890 --> 00:24:24.780
Araki...

00:24:25.330 --> 00:24:26.440
Who?

00:24:27.170 --> 00:24:29.190
Araki, so you've finally arrived...

00:24:39.490 --> 00:24:43.600
The magic show is about to begin.

00:24:45.940 --> 00:25:15.300
<b>Next Episode: Return of the King</b>

00:24:47.150 --> 00:24:48.970
Finally, the complete revival of the

00:24:48.970 --> 00:24:51.090
King of the Pitch, Ryuichi Araki.

00:24:51.090 --> 00:24:54.220
The long awaited magician's 
numerous wonderful plays

00:24:54.220 --> 00:24:55.720
stir surprise in Kakeru's heart.

00:24:56.110 --> 00:24:57.640
In response to FC's resurgence,

00:24:57.640 --> 00:25:00.710
SC's ace, Ryoma Oda,
 makes a decision

00:25:00.710 --> 00:25:02.230
in order to definitely win.

00:25:02.620 --> 00:25:04.790
The match reaches its climax.

00:25:04.790 --> 00:25:07.870
What will be the end of the drama 
that Kakeru and Araki create?

00:25:07.870 --> 00:25:09.520
Next time on Knight in the Area,

00:25:09.520 --> 00:25:12.140
episode 7: "Return of the King."

00:25:12.140 --> 00:25:15.650
I want to see the striker's 
stage that Kakeru makes.
